<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Fixture: a well-formed Torznab search response (T-021). Two invented
  items on an invented server; example.org only (AGENT.md §2).

  Item 1 carries every attribute this adapter reads, with peers greater
  than seeders (the total-peers reading — see DEC-065). Item 2 carries no
  magneturl at all, so it exercises the enclosure-only path, an RFC 1123
  "GMT" pubDate, and a verified rather than a vip trust attribute.

  The xmlns:torznab declaration a real server sends is omitted from every
  fixture here. Its value is an http URL on a host that is neither
  example.org nor a reserved TLD, and scripts/check-indexer-hostnames.sh
  scans testdata/ in full, so stating it would fail that check (backlog
  T-933). Nothing is lost: Go's encoding/xml accepts an undeclared prefix,
  and this adapter matches <attr> by local name regardless of namespace, so
  a prefixed element parses through exactly the same code path either way.
  TestAttrElementParsesUnderAnyNamespacePrefix proves both halves.
-->
